WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:19.453
On Tuesday morning, Luke and Carlos stood outside their fourth-grade classroom.

2
00:00:19.454 --> 00:00:22.770
"I've been thinking," said Carlos.

3
00:00:22.771 --> 00:00:28.293
"If we make up with Katie now, she'll make us square-dance."

4
00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.462
Luke raised his eyebrows.

5
00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.438
"So maybe we should make up after her report?"

6
00:00:34.439 --> 00:00:37.701
"Exactly," said Carlos.

7
00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:42.353
"Uh-oh," said Luke. "Here she comes."

8
00:00:42.354 --> 00:00:44.750
Katie was marching down the hall.

9
00:00:44.751 --> 00:00:49.122
Joy and the friendship meter were right behind her.

10
00:00:49.123 --> 00:00:52.106
"Guys!" called Katie.

11
00:00:52.107 --> 00:00:55.627
Luke groaned. "We're caught.

12
00:00:55.628 --> 00:01:00.151
Like rats in a trap."

13
00:01:00.152 --> 00:01:03.871
"I've come to say I'm sorry," Katie announced.

14
00:01:03.872 --> 00:01:06.744
She glanced at Joy, who nodded.

15
00:01:06.745 --> 00:01:08.992
"Sorry I missed practice.

16
00:01:08.993 --> 00:01:12.110
I should have watched the clock."

17
00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:14.996
"Carlos?" said Joy.

18
00:01:14.997 --> 00:01:17.296
Carlos looked down at his feet.

19
00:01:17.297 --> 00:01:21.102
"Sorry I got mad," he mumbled.

20
00:01:21.103 --> 00:01:23.985
"Luke?" said Joy.

21
00:01:23.986 --> 00:01:29.451
Luke sighed. "I shouldn't have hung up on you."

22
00:01:29.452 --> 00:01:32.722
Joy looked at the friendship meter.

23
00:01:32.723 --> 00:01:36.040
The pointer was on the smiling face.

24
00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:38.360
"That's good enough," she said.

25
00:01:38.361 --> 00:01:40.866
"I think you've made up now."

26
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.416
Luke and Carlos didn't say anything.

27
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:46.197
They just rushed into class.

28
00:01:46.198 --> 00:01:48.912
"That wasn't so bad," said Katie.

29
00:01:48.913 --> 00:01:51.679
"And I feel a lot better!"

30
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.984
"See?" Joy beamed.

31
00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:57.247
"Friendship is good for your health!"

32
00:01:57.248 --> 00:02:00.748
That afternoon, Olivia presented her report.

33
00:02:00.749 --> 00:02:04.897
She held up a poster with a big yellow sun.

34
00:02:04.898 --> 00:02:08.906
"You may think a tan looks good," she said.

35
00:02:08.907 --> 00:02:14.154
"But too much sun can cause burns now—and skin cancer later.

36
00:02:14.155 --> 00:02:16.903
So use sunscreen."

37
00:02:16.904 --> 00:02:19.301
Olivia held up another poster.

38
00:02:19.302 --> 00:02:23.701
"In Hawaii they have bugs called centipedes.

39
00:02:23.702 --> 00:02:29.179
They can grow to be thirty centimeters long, and they sting.

40
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:34.358
This black bug isn't a centipede. It's a tick."

41
00:02:34.359 --> 00:02:37.897
Katie smiled from ear to ear.

42
00:02:37.898 --> 00:02:45.102
"If you've been walking in tall grass," said Olivia, "check for ticks when you go inside."

43
00:02:45.103 --> 00:02:47.878
Olivia held up her last poster.

44
00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:53.155
"Poison ivy," she said.

45
00:02:53.156 --> 00:02:59.080
"If you see a plant like this—with three leaves—stay away.

46
00:02:59.081 --> 00:03:04.554
If you touch it, rush inside and wash with soap and water.

47
00:03:04.555 --> 00:03:07.997
Don't wait or it might be too late!"

48
00:03:07.998 --> 00:03:12.010
Then Olivia passed around a jar of hand cream.

49
00:03:12.011 --> 00:03:14.188
"Cream can protect your skin.

50
00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:17.329
This one is made from kukui nuts.

51
00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.075
Just like my necklace!

52
00:03:19.076 --> 00:03:21.514
Go ahead and try some."

53
00:03:21.515 --> 00:03:25.777
"Very nice report," said Ms. Barrow.

54
00:03:25.778 --> 00:03:28.085
Carlos was next.

55
00:03:28.086 --> 00:03:35.380
"If you didn't have ears," said Carlos, "you couldn't hear sirens, trains, or even tornadoes."

56
00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:40.881
"We wouldn't be able to hear you!" said Katie.

57
00:03:40.882 --> 00:03:43.088
"So you must protect your ears."

58
00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.719
Carlos looked at his note card.

59
00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.871
"Loud sounds can harm your ears.

60
00:03:48.872 --> 00:03:54.172
If other people can hear music from your earphones, the music is too loud."

61
00:03:54.173 --> 00:03:57.683
Carlos looked at his note card again.

62
00:03:57.684 --> 00:04:00.272
"Don't put anything pointy in your ears.

63
00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:04.099
In fact, don't put anything in your ears.

64
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.448
That's all," he said and returned to his desk.

65
00:04:08.449 --> 00:04:13.525
"Good report," whispered Katie. "Short and sweet."

66
00:04:13.526 --> 00:04:17.589
Luke's report on healthy eating was the last one of the day.

67
00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.421
He was serving snacks!

68
00:04:21.422 --> 00:04:26.282
"Food is like gasoline for our bodies!" said Luke.

69
00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:28.910
"We can't run without it."

70
00:04:28.911 --> 00:04:33.482
He unrolled a big poster and pinned it to the whiteboard.

71
00:04:33.483 --> 00:04:35.472
"This is a food pyramid.

72
00:04:35.473 --> 00:04:39.865
And these are snacks prepared by my mom at Fried Pie Heaven.

73
00:04:39.866 --> 00:04:42.998
They include all the food groups in the pyramid.

74
00:04:42.999 --> 00:04:48.846
Fruits, vegetables, grains, dairy, and nuts!"

75
00:04:48.847 --> 00:04:52.912
"Where are the fried pies?" asked Larry.

76
00:04:52.913 --> 00:04:58.339
Luke sighed. "I've got bad news," he said.

77
00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.930
"Fried pies are not on the pyramid."

78
00:05:01.931 --> 00:05:06.074
"WHAT?" cried the fourth graders.

79
00:05:06.075 --> 00:05:08.448
"They have too much fat and sugar.

80
00:05:08.449 --> 00:05:11.061
We shouldn't eat them very often.

81
00:05:11.062 --> 00:05:16.096
That's why my mom makes sure there are healthy foods on the menu too."

82
00:05:16.097 --> 00:05:18.833
"Dig in!" said Luke.

83
00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:24.600
While the fourth graders ate, Katie sneaked up behind Luke and Carlos.

84
00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:28.590
"Hi, guys!" she said with a big grin.

85
00:05:28.591 --> 00:05:31.469
"Is tonight okay for square-dance practice?

86
00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:37.477
My presentation is tomorrow!"
